Z||000000||hyhy4u||07-13-2001||12:05 PM||||My cars kindof strange...right when i change the oil the car wont smoke at all..but when i put like 800-1000 miles on after a oil change it gives out a HUGE! puff of smoke on start up and then dont smoke anymore...what causes this??||||reg||4
Z||000001||LAMBO||07-13-2001||12:15 PM||||My guess would be old, brittle valve guide seals. Common on most engines with higher miles. Unless it really bothers you, I wouldn't worry about it too much, it's not really hurting anything.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||07-13-2001||12:40 PM||||if you check back in archives, youll see almost everyone has the same problem on startup. Dont worry about it. Mines done it since new engine, still runs perfect after 85,000 miles. I just think its the nature of the particular engine. You might check in the air cleaner housing to see if your getting any accumulation of oil residue from blowby.||||reg||1
